          ],
          "content": "Light Emitting Diode (LED) lamps are modern light sources that consume much less power, are brighter and last longer than traditional lamps. This notand last longer than traditional lamps. This not only reduces electricity bills but is also better foronly reduces electricity bills but is also better for environment. Recognising their advantages, theenvironment. Recognising their advantages, the Indian government has made substantial efforts toIndian government has made substantial efforts to promote the use of LED lamps nationwide. At theirpromote the use of LED lamps nationwide. At their end of life, LED lamps must be appropriately disposedend of life, LED lamps must be appropriately disposed or recycled, and not thrown in the garbage.or recycled, and not thrown in the garbage."
